From: Baolin Wang <baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:12:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm: mglru: use pte_table_clamped_end() helper to calculate
 the end

Use pte_table_clamped_end() to clamp the range to the PTE table and VMA
boundaries when batch-checking young flags, making the code more readable.

No functional changes intended.

Link: https://patch.msgid.link/b2386c5da61f9a15e60daa421b033bc1e0bcdd41.1794481498.git.baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com
Signed-off-by: Baolin Wang <baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>
Cc: Johannes Weiner <hannes@cmpxchg.org>
Cc: Kairui Song <kasong@tencent.com>
Cc: Barry Song <baohua@kernel.org>
Cc: Axel Rasmussen <axelrasmussen@google.com>
Cc: Yuanchu Xie <yuanchu@google.com>
Cc: Wei Xu <weixugc@google.com>
Cc: Baoquan He <baoquan.he@linux.dev>
Cc: Qi Zheng <qi.zheng@linux.dev>
Cc: Shakeel Butt <shakeel.butt@linux.dev>
Cc: Michal Hocko <mhocko@kernel.org>

 mm/vmscan.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index fe1fe1439c7c..bc7579d47f9b 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -4343,7 +4343,7 @@ bool lru_gen_look_around(struct page_vma_mapped_walk *pvmw, unsigned int nr)
 	walk = current->reclaim_state ? current->reclaim_state->mm_walk : NULL;
 
 	start = max(addr & PMD_MASK, vma->vm_start);
-	end = min(addr | ~PMD_MASK, vma->vm_end - 1) + 1;
+	end = pte_table_clamped_end(addr, vma->vm_end);
 
 	if (end - start == PAGE_SIZE)
 		return true;
-- 
